{"parentUuid":"6d275bba-6381-4793-b0e3-8d8f35fb24af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a4f5cad1-499a-4db8-8e81-10d7a66fd642","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"can you read this report / debug session:\n\nWhat's there\n\n  - 17/813205bbce/ has two sessions: 0/ = Codex (agent: \"Codex\", model gpt-5.4, session 019dba89…), 1/ = Claude Code (agent: \"Claude Code\", 10 checkpoints, 737-line transcript).\n  - Codex's 0/ contains only metadata.json — no full.jsonl, no prompt.txt, no content_hash.txt. Top-level sessions[0].prompt is even explicitly \"\".\n\n  So Codex was a first-class session. It was registered and condensed — just with nothing to condense.\n\n  Why 0/ is empty\n\n  The session-state file .git/entire-sessions/019dba89-44d8-79f1-8151-b605e6a3c7d2.json gives it away:\n\n  \"phase\": \"active\",\n  \"checkpoint_count\": 0,\n  \"last_prompt\": \"<role> You are Codex performing an adversarial software review...\"\n\n  - checkpoint_count: 0 — no SaveStep ever fired for this Codex turn. The shadow branch never got .entire/metadata/019dba89…/full.jsonl or prompt.txt written to it.\n  - phase: \"active\" — the session never transitioned to idle/ended. Stop hook never cleanly closed it.\n  - Yet base_commit, last_prompt, and agent/model fields are populated, so something wired Codex into Entire at session start, just not at turn end.\n\n  What condensation did\n\n  At commit time, condenseSessions walks session-state files and writes a <N>/metadata.json per session — that's why 0/metadata.json exists (and carries agent_lines: 0, agent_removed: 228, human_removed: 849 — those come from a base_commit\n   → HEAD diff, not from the transcript). When it went to copy transcript files from .entire/metadata/019dba89…/ on the shadow branch, that dir was empty, so full.jsonl / prompt.txt / content_hash.txt simply weren't produced.\n\n  The prompt.txt miss is particularly telling: last_prompt is right there in session state, but the checkpoint dir gets its prompt from shadow-branch prompt.txt, not from session state.\n\n  Root cause\n\n  This is a bug in the Codex agent integration (still IsPreview: true in cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/codex.go:51). When /codex:adversarial-review runs Codex:\n\n  1. Something creates the Entire session state — likely Codex's SessionStart/init hook, which stores last_prompt and agent_type: \"Codex\".\n  2. Codex does its review work and exits.\n  3. The per-turn snapshot path that should write .entire/metadata/<codex-session-id>/full.jsonl + prompt.txt on the shadow branch (via SaveStep) never runs — either because the Stop hook doesn't fire in the subagent flow, or because the\n  rollout-to-metadata copy step is missing/short-circuiting.\n  4. Claude Code's own turn completes normally (1/ gets the full treatment).\n  5. User commits → condensation → Claude Code's session is fully copied; Codex's session contributes only the metadata.json stub.\n\n  If you want real Codex transcripts in future checkpoints, the fix is in the Codex agent wiring — probably its Stop-equivalent handler needs to read ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*-019dba89….jsonl and persist a snippet into the\n  shadow branch's .entire/metadata/<codex-session>/full.jsonl (and prompt.txt) the way Claude Code does.\n\nIf you need to look at a commit / checkpoint look at commit be7ff386a38c354805957294833a43f816267f5f in ../entiredb\n\nNow I want us to focus on two things: \n\n1. can we prevent this happening at all, like why are we writing `0/metadata.json` and there is no session log, we should not do this at all. There should never be a session without a session log, can we hard guard this somewhere? Or is this needed since the log might come later?\n2. can we figure out a way to handle this better and/or debug why the codex subsession hooks are not firing?"},"uuid":"3f44ab8d-52c8-4a3a-9d7d-0b605a2af63f","timestamp":"2026-04-23T17:46:59.244Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"c2a51e7d-ab7f-4f50-9349-537240c8648f","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"soph/empty-session-guard"}
