{"parentUuid":"d8c6cc10-aee1-4afa-b58d-1bf7bd0ed4d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a4f5cad1-499a-4db8-8e81-10d7a66fd642","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018z6Rv7aSh8rypz49YcSr7X","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t\n151\t### Hook Output (stdout JSON)\n152\t\n153\tAll hooks accept optional JSON output on stdout. Empty output is valid.\n154\t\n155\t**Universal fields (all events):**\n156\t```json\n157\t{\n158\t  \"continue\": true,\n159\t  \"stopReason\": null,\n160\t  \"suppressOutput\": false,\n161\t  \"systemMessage\": \"Optional message to display\"\n162\t}\n163\t```\n164\t\n165\tThe `systemMessage` field can be used to display messages to the user via the agent (similar to Claude Code's `systemMessage`).\n166\t\n167\t## Transcript\n168\t\n169\t- Location: JSONL \"rollout\" files in `~/.codex/` (sharded directory structure)\n170\t- Path pattern: `~/.codex/rollouts/<shard>/<shard>/rollout-<timestamp>-<thread-id>.jsonl`\n171\t- The `transcript_path` field in hook payloads provides the exact path\n172\t- Format: JSONL (line-delimited JSON)\n173\t- Session ID extraction: `session_id` field from hook payload (UUID format)\n174\t- Transcript may be null in `--ephemeral` mode\n175\t\n176\t**Note:** Codex's primary storage is SQLite (`~/.codex/state`), but the JSONL rollout file is the file-based transcript we can read. The `transcript_path` in hook payloads points to this file.\n177\t\n178\t## Config Preservation\n179\t\n180\t- Use read-modify-write on entire `hooks.json` file\n181\t- Preserve unknown keys in the `hooks` object (future event types)\n182\t- The `hooks.json` is separate from `config.toml` — safe to create/modify independently\n183\t\n184\t## CLI Flags\n185\t\n186\t- Non-interactive prompt: `codex exec \"<prompt>\"` or `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \"<prompt>\"`\n187\t- Interactive mode: `codex` or `codex \"<prompt>\"` (starts TUI)\n188\t- Resume session: `codex resume <session-id>` or `codex resume --last`\n189\t- Model override: `-m <model>` or `--model <model>`\n190\t- Full-auto mode: `codex exec --full-auto \"<prompt>\"` (workspace-write sandbox + auto-approve)\n191\t- JSONL output: `codex exec --json \"<prompt>\"` (events to stdout)\n192\t- Relevant env vars: `CODEX_HOME` (config dir override), `OPENAI_API_KEY` (API auth)\n193\t\n194\t## Gaps & Limitations\n195\t\n196\t- **Hooks require feature flag:** The `codex_hooks` feature is `default_enabled: false` (stage: UnderDevelopment). It must be enabled via `--enable codex_hooks` CLI flag, or `features.codex_hooks = true` in `config.toml`, or `-c features.codex_hooks=true`. Without this, hooks.json is ignored entirely.\n197\t- **No SessionEnd hook:** Codex does not fire a hook when a session is completely terminated. The `Stop` hook fires at end-of-turn, not end-of-session. This is similar to some other agents — the framework handles this gracefully.\n198\t- **PreToolUse is shell-only:** Currently only fires for `Bash` tool (direct shell execution). MCP tools, stdin streaming, and other tool types are not yet hooked. PostToolUse is in review.\n199\t- **Transcript may be null:** In `--ephemeral` mode, `transcript_path` is null. The integration should handle this gracefully.\n200\t- **No subagent hooks:** No PreTask/PostTask equivalent for subagent spawning.\n201\t- **Hook response protocol differs from Claude Code:** Codex uses `systemMessage` (same field name) but also supports `hookSpecificOutput` with `additionalContext` for injecting context into the model. For Entire's purposes, `systemMessage` is sufficient.\n202\t\n203\t## Captured Payloads\n204\t\n205\t- JSON schemas at `codex-rs/hooks/schema/generated/` in the Codex repository\n206\t- Hook config structure at `codex-rs/hooks/src/engine/config.rs` in the Codex repository\n207\t"}]},"uuid":"6bcb6360-1d03-4a1a-8808-d07afd458851","timestamp":"2026-04-23T17:57:01.492Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md","content":"\n### Hook Output (stdout JSON)\n\nAll hooks accept optional JSON output on stdout. Empty output is valid.\n\n**Universal fields (all events):**\n```json\n{\n  \"continue\": true,\n  \"stopReason\": null,\n  \"suppressOutput\": false,\n  \"systemMessage\": \"Optional message to display\"\n}\n```\n\nThe `systemMessage` field can be used to display messages to the user via the agent (similar to Claude Code's `systemMessage`).\n\n## Transcript\n\n- Location: JSONL \"rollout\" files in `~/.codex/` (sharded directory structure)\n- Path pattern: `~/.codex/rollouts/<shard>/<shard>/rollout-<timestamp>-<thread-id>.jsonl`\n- The `transcript_path` field in hook payloads provides the exact path\n- Format: JSONL (line-delimited JSON)\n- Session ID extraction: `session_id` field from hook payload (UUID format)\n- Transcript may be null in `--ephemeral` mode\n\n**Note:** Codex's primary storage is SQLite (`~/.codex/state`), but the JSONL rollout file is the file-based transcript we can read. The `transcript_path` in hook payloads points to this file.\n\n## Config Preservation\n\n- Use read-modify-write on entire `hooks.json` file\n- Preserve unknown keys in the `hooks` object (future event types)\n- The `hooks.json` is separate from `config.toml` — safe to create/modify independently\n\n## CLI Flags\n\n- Non-interactive prompt: `codex exec \"<prompt>\"` or `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \"<prompt>\"`\n- Interactive mode: `codex` or `codex \"<prompt>\"` (starts TUI)\n- Resume session: `codex resume <session-id>` or `codex resume --last`\n- Model override: `-m <model>` or `--model <model>`\n- Full-auto mode: `codex exec --full-auto \"<prompt>\"` (workspace-write sandbox + auto-approve)\n- JSONL output: `codex exec --json \"<prompt>\"` (events to stdout)\n- Relevant env vars: `CODEX_HOME` (config dir override), `OPENAI_API_KEY` (API auth)\n\n## Gaps & Limitations\n\n- **Hooks require feature flag:** The `codex_hooks` feature is `default_enabled: false` (stage: UnderDevelopment). It must be enabled via `--enable codex_hooks` CLI flag, or `features.codex_hooks = true` in `config.toml`, or `-c features.codex_hooks=true`. Without this, hooks.json is ignored entirely.\n- **No SessionEnd hook:** Codex does not fire a hook when a session is completely terminated. The `Stop` hook fires at end-of-turn, not end-of-session. This is similar to some other agents — the framework handles this gracefully.\n- **PreToolUse is shell-only:** Currently only fires for `Bash` tool (direct shell execution). MCP tools, stdin streaming, and other tool types are not yet hooked. PostToolUse is in review.\n- **Transcript may be null:** In `--ephemeral` mode, `transcript_path` is null. The integration should handle this gracefully.\n- **No subagent hooks:** No PreTask/PostTask equivalent for subagent spawning.\n- **Hook response protocol differs from Claude Code:** Codex uses `systemMessage` (same field name) but also supports `hookSpecificOutput` with `additionalContext` for injecting context into the model. For Entire's purposes, `systemMessage` is sufficient.\n\n## Captured Payloads\n\n- JSON schemas at `codex-rs/hooks/schema/generated/` in the Codex repository\n- Hook config structure at `codex-rs/hooks/src/engine/config.rs` in the Codex repository\n","numLines":58,"startLine":150,"totalLines":207}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8c6cc10-aee1-4afa-b58d-1bf7bd0ed4d0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"c2a51e7d-ab7f-4f50-9349-537240c8648f","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"soph/empty-session-guard"}
