{"parentUuid":"ebd705cb-eeec-44e4-9273-667b27434dc0","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"We're investigating why a Codex session wrote a stub `0/metadata.json` with no transcript and why its Stop hook apparently never fired. Next action is adding lifecycle-hook logging so the next repro tells us which of five possible failure modes actually hit. (disable recaps in /config)","timestamp":"2026-04-23T19:13:16.429Z","uuid":"ef4cc582-2ebc-46c1-b9ab-94d696c64d2c","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"c2a51e7d-ab7f-4f50-9349-537240c8648f","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"soph/empty-session-guard"}
{"type":"file-history-snapshot","messageId":"ee2391f2-93a2-4a27-9b3d-488d4f2051a5","snapshot":{"messageId":"ee2391f2-93a2-4a27-9b3d-488d4f2051a5","trackedFileBackups":{},"timestamp":"2026-04-24T08:07:34.465Z"},"isSnapshotUpdate":false}
{"parentUuid":"ef4cc582-2ebc-46c1-b9ab-94d696c64d2c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2ae183c4-ca9a-42fd-9860-7b0380811abf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I chatted with the reporter again, we were wondering if maybe ctrl+c was used, but here is the analysi:\n\n:black_circle_for_record: Short answer: no evidence you hit ctrl-C on the Claude Code session itself. The Codex side is suspicious, but the fingerprint points more at missing integration than at an interrupt.\n\n  What the artifacts say:\n\n  Claude Code (28c2a1e4) — clean run:\n  - 865 transcript lines spanning 13:05:23Z → 14:47:17Z (1h42m)\n  - Stop reasons: 337 tool_use, 24 end_turn, 1 stop_sequence — no \"interrupted\":true, no SIGINT/SIGTERM/abort markers\n  - 11 turns, 10 checkpoints, condensed normally at commit time (14:09Z)\n  - Only 2 BashOutput reads across 3 /codex:adversarial-review launches — you fired them and barely looked at them, but CC itself finished naturally\n\n  The three Codex sessions — frozen at birth:\n\n  ┌──────────┬───────────────┬──────────────────┬──────┐\n  │ session  │ started (UTC) │ last_interaction │  Δ   │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────┼──────────────────┼──────┤\n  │ 019dba69 │ 12:56:07.561  │ 12:56:07.562     │ ~1ms │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────┼──────────────────┼──────┤\n  │ 019dba89 │ 13:30:54.573  │ 13:30:54.576     │ ~3ms │\n  ├──────────┼───────────────┼──────────────────┼──────┤\n  │ 019dbabf │ 14:29:54.379  │ 14:29:54.380     │ ~1ms │\n  └──────────┴───────────────┴──────────────────┴──────┘\n\n  All three: phase: \"active\", checkpoint_count: 0, last_interaction_time literally microseconds after started_at. That means Codex's SessionStart-equivalent fired once to register the session, and then no other Entire hook ever ran for\n  those sessions. No UserPromptSubmit, no Stop, no PostCommit.\n\n  And no rollout files exist at all — ~/.codex/sessions/2026/04/23/ doesn't exist (dir jumps 22 → 01/01 the other way). That's true for all three launches, not just one.\n\n  Why this isn't a ctrl-C story:\n  If you'd ctrl-C'd the CC session, the CC transcript would typically show an abort marker and you'd expect only later codex subprocesses to die; the first one (12:56Z) had 1h50m to run before CC exited. Three identical microsecond-gap\n  start/stop windows in three different sessions is a systematic pattern, not a one-off interrupt.\n\n  The more likely story: Codex's Entire integration (still IsPreview: true) registers a session at launch but its turn-end handler — the one that's supposed to read ~/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-*.jsonl and write snippets into\n  .entire/metadata/<codex-session>/full.jsonl on the shadow branch — isn't running, at least not in the codex-companion.mjs subprocess path used by /codex:adversarial-review. That also explains why no rollout files exist at all for that\n  day: the companion likely runs Codex with some output-capture mode (or a different CODEX_HOME) that bypasses the normal session directory, so neither Codex's own rollout nor Entire's mirror of it ever lands on disk.\n\n  If you want to be extra sure it wasn't ctrl-C: check your shell history for that window — ctrl-C in CC often leaves a partial command line on disk — and see if /codex:status on 2026-04-23 reported completions."},"uuid":"ee2391f2-93a2-4a27-9b3d-488d4f2051a5","timestamp":"2026-04-24T08:07:28.099Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"c2a51e7d-ab7f-4f50-9349-537240c8648f","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
