{"parentUuid":"26da7a0c-01cf-456c-8908-8404301f42fc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t# Entire - CLI\n2\t\n3\tThis repo contains the CLI for Entire.\n4\t\n5\t## Architecture\n6\t\n7\t- CLI built with github.com/spf13/cobra and github.com/charmbracelet/huh\n8\t\n9\t## Key Directories\n10\t\n11\t### Commands (`cmd/`)\n12\t\n13\t- `entire/`: Main CLI entry point\n14\t- `entire/cli`: CLI utilities and helpers\n15\t- `entire/cli/commands`: actual command implementations\n16\t- `entire/cli/agent`: agent implementations (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI) - see [Agent Integration Checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) and [Agent Implementation Guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md)\n17\t- `entire/cli/strategy`: strategy implementation (manual-commit) - see section below\n18\t- `entire/cli/checkpoint`: checkpoint storage abstractions (temporary and committed)\n19\t- `entire/cli/session`: session state management\n20\t- `entire/cli/integration_test`: integration tests (simulated hooks)\n21\t- `e2e/`: E2E tests with real agent calls (see [e2e/README.md](e2e/README.md))\n22\t\n23\t## Tech Stack\n24\t\n25\t- Language: Go 1.26.x\n26\t- Build tool: mise, go modules\n27\t- Linting: golangci-lint\n28\t\n29\t## Development\n30\t\n31\t### Running Tests\n32\t\n33\t```bash\n34\tmise run test\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\t### Running Integration Tests\n38\t\n39\t```bash\n40\tmise run test:integration\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\t### Running All Tests (CI)\n44\t\n45\t```bash\n46\tmise run test:ci\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tThis runs unit tests, integration tests, and the E2E canary (Vogon agent) in sequence. Integration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n50\t\n51\t### Running E2E Canary Tests (Vogon Agent)\n52\t\n53\tThe Vogon agent is a deterministic fake agent that exercises the full E2E test suite without making any API calls. Named after the Vogons from The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy — bureaucratic, procedural, and deterministic to a fault.\n54\t\n55\t```bash\n56\tmise run test:e2e:canary           # Run all E2E tests with the Vogon agent\n57\tmise run test:e2e:canary TestFoo   # Run a specific test\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t- **Runs as part of `test:ci`** — canary failures block merges\n61\t- **No API calls, no cost** — safe to run freely, unlike real agent E2E tests\n62\t- **If a canary test fails, the bug is in the CLI or test infrastructure**, not in an agent\n63\t- Located in `e2e/vogon/` (binary) and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/vogon/` (Agent interface)\n64\t- The binary parses prompts via regex, creates/modifies/deletes files, and fires lifecycle hooks\n65\t- **IMPORTANT: When changing E2E test prompt wording**, the Vogon binary (`e2e/vogon/main.go`) parses prompts with hardcoded regexes. New phrasing may not match existing patterns — always run `mise run test:e2e:canary` after changing prompt text and fix Vogon's parsing if tests fail.\n66\t\n67\t### Running E2E Tests (Only When Explicitly Requested)\n68\t\n69\t**IMPORTANT: Do NOT run E2E tests proactively.** E2E tests make real API calls to agents, which consume tokens and cost money. Only run them when the user explicitly asks for E2E testing.\n70\t\n71\t```bash\n72\tmise run test:e2e [filter]                          # All agents, filtered\n73\tmise run test:e2e --agent claude-code [filter]       # Claude Code only\n74\tmise run test:e2e --agent gemini-cli [filter]        # Gemini CLI only\n75\tmise run test:e2e --agent opencode [filter]          # OpenCode only\n76\tmise run test:e2e --agent cursor [filter]            # Cursor only\n77\tmise run test:e2e --agent factoryai-droid [filter]   # Factory AI Droid only\n78\tmise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli [filter]       # Copilot CLI only\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\tE2E tests:\n82\t\n83\t- Use the `//go:build e2e` build tag\n84\t- Located in `e2e/tests/`\n85\t- See [`e2e/README.md`](e2e/README.md) for full documentation (structure, debugging, adding agents)\n86\t- Test real agent interactions (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, or Vogon creating files, committing, etc.)\n87\t- Validate checkpoint scenarios documented in `docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md`\n88\t- Support multiple agents via `E2E_AGENT` env var (`claude-code`, `gemini`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `factoryai-droid`, `copilot-cli`, `vogon`)\n89\t\n90\t**Environment variables:**\n91\t\n92\t- `E2E_AGENT` - Agent to test with (default: `claude-code`)\n93\t- `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` - Claude model to use (default: `haiku` for cost efficiency)\n94\t- `E2E_TIMEOUT` - Timeout per prompt (default: `2m`)\n95\t\n96\t### Test Parallelization\n97\t\n98\t**Always use `t.Parallel()` in tests.** Every top-level test function and subtest should call `t.Parallel()` unless it modifies process-global state (e.g., `os.Chdir()`).\n99\t\n100\t```go\n101\tfunc TestFeature_Foo(t *testing.T) {\n102\t    t.Parallel()\n103\t    // ...\n104\t}\n105\t\n106\t// Integration tests with TestEnv\n107\tfunc TestFeature_Bar(t *testing.T) {\n108\t    t.Parallel()\n109\t    env := NewFeatureBranchEnv(t)\n110\t    // ...\n111\t}\n112\t```\n113\t\n114\t**Exception:** Tests that modify process-global state cannot be parallelized. This includes `os.Chdir()`/`t.Chdir()` and `os.Setenv()`/`t.Setenv()` — Go's test framework will panic if these are used after `t.Parallel()`.\n115\t\n116\t### Git in Tests\n117\t\n118\t**Tests that touch git state must use an isolated temp repo — never the real repo CWD.**\n119\t\n120\tMany handlers (lifecycle, strategy, hooks) resolve the git repo from CWD via `OpenRepository`, `GetGitCommonDir`, `DetectFileChanges`, etc. Without isolation, tests can create session state files, shadow branches, or other artifacts in the real `.git/` directory.\n121\t\n122\tUse the `testutil` helpers:\n123\t\n124\t```go\n125\t