isibility into until someone reads `codex-companion.mjs`\n\n**Revised filing/fix recommendation.** If timeout is the dominant pattern, what you want from Codex is the same ask I suggested earlier but with a better repro: \"when the Codex process is terminated externally (SIGTERM) during a turn, there's no cleanup hook — downstream integrations have no way to know the session ended. Would be useful to (a) install a SIGTERM handler that fires Stop with an interrupted status, or (b) expose a SessionEnd hook that fires unconditionally on process exit.\" That's a concrete, testable ask they can say yes or no to.\n\nOn our side, the rollout-reconciliation fallback I suggested before becomes the primary fix regardless: at condense time, for ACTIVE external-agent sessions with a known `TranscriptPath`, read the rollout (if present), extract what we can, and finalize the session. That covers both \"Codex crashed\" and \"Codex was killed by timeout\" without needing upstream changes.\n\nShort version: yes, timeout is a better story than the error-path theory was, and probably better than pure ephemeral. Reading `codex-companion.mjs` would disambiguate definitively — want me to look for it in the usual places?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223036,"cache_read_input_tokens":29258,"output_tokens":3796,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":223036,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3796,"cache_read_input_tokens":29258,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":223036},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaNSXRqLZs8SvLCu34EmR","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd917c15-06af-4d47-8313-e59a47909385","timestamp":"2026-04-24T10:31:22.035Z","userTy