{"parentUuid":"fdf48045-1643-4059-b8e8-d83e256ae1ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2ad96ba5-60e0-4144-8d65-33e09ec75227","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"but more data: \n\n[codex] Running command: /bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba cmd/worker/syncer.go | sed -n '60,140p'\"\n     [codex] Command completed: /bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba cmd/worker/syncer.go | sed -n '60,140p'\" (exit 0)\n     [codex] Running command: /bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba cmd/worker/syncer_test.go | sed -n '220,360p'\"\n     [codex] Command completed: /bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba cmd/worker/syncer_test.go | sed -n '220,360p'\" (exit 0)\n     [codex] Assistant message captured: {\"verdict\":\"needs-attention\",\"summary\":\"No-ship: the new redirect auth logic relies on an uns...\n     [codex] Turn completed.\n     # Codex Adversarial Review\n\n     Target: working tree diff\n     Verdict: needs-attention\n\n     No-ship: the new redirect auth logic relies on an unsafe DNS heuristic, so it can leak the mirror key to a broader host set and still fail on valid cluster topologies.\n\n     Findings:\n     - [high] Cluster membership is inferred with a brittle suffix heuristic that widens the trust boundary and misses some legitimate sibling redirects (cmd/worker/syncer.go:90-126)\n       `clusterFQDN` strips the first label from any 4+ label target host, and `hostInCluster` then treats any hostname ending in `.`+cluster as trusted. That is not equivalent to 'the configured cluster and its direct replicas'. For\n     example, a 4-label cluster entry host like `mirror.prod.example.com` is broadened to `prod.example.com`, so redirects to unrelated siblings under that parent zone would receive `X-Entire-Mirror-Key`. The opposite failure also\n     exists: a node-specific 3-label host like `node1.cluster.local` is left unchanged, so a redirect to `node2.cluster.local` still drops auth and reproduces the original 401. This is an inference from the code plus the documented\n     `ENTIRE_TARGET_URL` contract: the config does not constrain hostnames to the one shape this heuristic assumes. The result is a silent trust-boundary regression in some deployments and a silent auth regression in others.\n       Recommendation: Do not derive cluster identity from label count. Pass the authoritative cluster FQDN explicitly, or reuse the server/discovery implementation that defines valid same-cluster hosts. If matching remains local,\n     restrict it to the exact cluster host or exactly one replica label, and add tests for 3-label node hosts, 4-label cluster entry domains, and deeper subdomains.\n\n     Next steps:\n     - Replace `clusterFQDN`/`hostInCluster` with an explicit cluster host matcher from authoritative config or shared discovery code.\n     - Add regression tests covering nested subdomains, 3-label node hostnames, and 4+-label cluster entry domains before shipping this redirect behavior.\n  ⎿  (timeout 10m)\n  ⎿  1 PostToolUse hook ran\n\nThis is strange, so it shows a timeout but also that codex finished... I feel there should have been a hook fired"},"uuid":"9c5ab5c7-0ab1-4beb-a047-26915b9cd8cb","timestamp":"2026-04-24T10:34:53.972Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"c2a51e7d-ab7f-4f50-9349-537240c8648f","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
