{"parentUuid":"1b2aabe2-b9de-4dd2-8902-a054d69898d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017qwgmERdVFNRb1bgr5vrgZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — this is the killing blow for the earlier theories. The log sequence tells us exactly what happened:\n\n```\n[codex] Turn completed.      ← Codex's internal turn loop finished\n# Codex Adversarial Review   ← final message streamed to stdout\n...\n⎿  (timeout 10m)             ← Claude Code's Bash tool fired SIGKILL\n```\n\nCodex reached turn completion, which means control reached `turn.rs:537` and **Stop was dispatched** (that line fires before the `break;` that leads to \"Turn completed\"). So the Stop hook *was* invoked. It just never had a chance to finish.\n\n## Why the state still looks post-TurnStart-only\n\nLook at the order of operations in `lifecycle.go:handleLifecycleTurnEnd`:\n\n1. Check `transcriptRef != \"\"` (bail if empty)\n2. `PrepareTranscript` / `fileExists` check\n3. Create session dir, read transcript, copy to session dir\n4. Load pre-prompt state, resolve offsets\n5. Backfill prompt.txt\n6. ... detect file changes ...\n7. **SaveStep** — this is where `state.FilesTouched` gets merged, shadow branch commit gets built\n8. **TransitionAndLog(EventTurnEnd)** — only *here* does `ActionUpdateLastInteraction` fire and `LastInteractionTime` move\n\n`LastInteractionTime` is only bumped at step 8. If SIGKILL hit anywhere from step 1 through step 7 — which is everything expensive: the transcript copy, the go-git shadow commit, the redact pass — you'd see exactly what the reporter found: `checkpoint_count: 0`, no shadow branch content, `LastInteractionTime` still at the TurnStart value from 10 minutes earlier.\n\n## What the 10m timeout actually kills\n\nClaude Code's Bash tool timeout kills the entire process tree, not just Codex. That includes `entire hooks codex stop`, which is a child of the Codex process. Between Codex's Stop dispatch (